  "body": "# 🌟 IRIS-MINI Neural Core - v1.1.1\r\n\r\nWe are thrilled to announce the official release of **IRIS-MINI v1.1.1**. This update brings major stability improvements to the CLI Core, ensuring flawless execution across global environments and silencing backend telemetry for a pristine terminal experience.\r\n\r\n## 🚀 What's New & Improved\r\n\r\n* **Absolute Pathing Engine:** Completely overhauled the Express server routing. The UI now resolves perfectly regardless of where the CLI is executed globally.\r\n* **The Silence Protocol:** Integrated strict Node.js hook interceptors. All internal V8 deprecation warnings (DEP0205) and Vite dev-logs are now completely masked in production.\r\n* **Express v5 Compatibility:** Updated routing wildcard logic (`/.*/`) to comply with the new `path-to-regexp` strictness in Express 5.1.0.\r\n* **Terminal UX Enhancements:** Added an explicit `Ctrl + C` exit command indicator to the boot banner for better user control.\r\n\r\n## 📦 Installation Instructions\r\n\r\nThere are two ways to install this release. \r\n\r\n### Option 1: The NPM Registry (Recommended)\r\nFor the fastest and easiest installation, pull directly from the global registry:\r\n```bash\r\nnpm install -g iris-mini@1.1.1\r\n```"
